    <section class="col-lg-9">
        <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm">
            <div class="card-body p-4 p-lg-5">
                <div class="azure-notes-content">
                    <pre class="azure-notes-text">What is the CI/CD Pipeline in Azure?
A CI/CD pipeline in Azure automates the process of integrating code changes and deploying
applications. It ensures that every code change is built, tested, and deployed automatically, helping
developers catch issues early and deliver updates faster without manual intervention.

    •     Continuous Integration (CI): Automatically integrates code changes and triggers builds/tests
          with every commit.

    •     Continuous Delivery (CD): Automates the deployment process to different environments like
          staging or production.

    •     Automated Testing: Run automated tests to verify code quality before deploying.

    •     Version Control Integration: Works seamlessly with GitHub, Azure Repos, and other version
          control systems.

    •     Multi-Platform Support: Supports deployment on various platforms such as Windows, Linux,
          and macOS.

    •     Scalability: Handles projects of all sizes, from small apps to enterprise-level systems.</pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    

            @await Html.PartialAsync("~/Areas/Azure/Views/Shared/AzureLessonNavigation.cshtml")
</section>
</div>
